-- title:
--   Finite convex approximations with prefix coefficients
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals.
--
--   1. **Closed convex hulls.** A point of $\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\,D$ is within $\tau$ of a finite convex combination $\sum_{i<q}w_id_i$ of points of $D$, $q\ge1$.
--   2. **Prefix form.** For a sequence $u$, a point of $\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\{u_n\}$ is within $\tau$ of
--   $$
--   \sum_{i<N}\beta_iu_i ,
--   $$
--   with coefficients on a whole initial segment. Missing indices get weight $0$.
--   3. **Ordered reindexing.** Enumerating a finite set of indices increasingly preserves all sums, so zero coefficients can be dropped without changing order.
